# --- Secrets / environment (NEVER commit) ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.local

# --- Commercial / legal material (deliberately NOT in this repo) ---
# Pricing, setup fees, discounting policy, contract terms and the open
# legal-entity question. Kept out for a specific reason, not just tidiness:
# the SERVER pulls this repo, so committing it would place commercial terms on
# the production box for no operational benefit. "It is a private repo" is not
# the control you want protecting this -- that lasts exactly until the first
# collaborator is added.
#
# The engineering content that used to live alongside it has been extracted:
#   docs/engineering-lessons.md   (the tests-that-pass-wrongly pattern)
#   docs/concierge-runbook.md §6  (conditions on the n8n env-access decision)
# If you add commercial material to that doc, it stays here. If you add
# ENGINEERING material to it, port the engineering part into docs/ instead --
# otherwise it becomes invisible to anyone working from the repo.
ryvo-operations-and-commercial-reference.md

# --- Backups (DB dumps live outside git history) ---
# /backups/* ignores the dumps; backups/n8n/ (the nightly workflow export) is
# tracked and pushed offsite. tests/backup_target.test.sh proves a dump stays ignored.
/backups/*
!/backups/n8n/

# --- Node / tooling ---
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# --- Legal documents ---
#
# The repo is code, and it syncs to GitHub. Contracts live with the other legal
# documents outside it (operator, 23 Sep 2026).
#
# 🔒 THE OUTPUT LEAVES; THE SOURCE STAYS. legal/fonte/ holds the markdown these
# documents are written in and legal/typeset.py is what renders them, so the
# repo keeps everything needed to produce a document and none of the documents
# themselves. The eight rendered PDFs were untracked when this rule was added.
#
# 🔴 BY FILE TYPE, NOT BY DIRECTORY, and that distinction is load-bearing:
# legal/modelos/ holds modelos-whatsapp.md BESIDE its rendered PDF, so ignoring
# the output directories would have taken a source with them.
legal/**/*.pdf

# --- Python build output ---
#
# 🔴 One .pyc was already COMMITTED before this rule existed:
# infra/scripts/__pycache__/metrics_daily.cpython-314.pyc, carried in since
# 9552815. Bytecode is a build artefact of a .py that has since changed, so a
# fresh checkout got a file that no longer matched its source. Untracked at the
# same time as this line was added (23 Sep 2026).
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- Local tool state, not the project's ---
# Per-machine permissions for the agent tooling. It is not configuration the
# project shares, and it changes on whichever machine is being used.
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- OS / editor cruft ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# cockpit
cockpit/node_modules/
cockpit/.next/
cockpit/.env*.local
cockpit/next-env.d.ts
cockpit/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
cockpit/.vercel/
.vercel
tests/*.SABOTAGE.json
.playwright-mcp
/tmp-shots/

# The deploy-gate copy of the Concierge: generated per gate run by tests/build_gate.py.
tests/*.GATE.json
